### Description

Fetch the approval content of an approval task, so that the **approval channel** can create a ticket and present it to the approver. This is an **application-authenticated API**.

Caller restrictions (any mismatch is reported as "approval task does not exist", without distinguishing "does not exist" from "no permission"):

- The caller must be **the application of the approval channel assigned to the task**;
- The user passed in the `X-Bk-Username` header must be **the creator of the approval task**;
- The tenant that user belongs to must match the tenant of the approval task.

The channel must therefore fetch the content as **the current approver** and must not always pass a fixed account. This API **does not accept self-service permission applications** and can only be called after being granted by the Job platform administrator.

The approval content `approval_content` is **Markdown already rendered by the Job platform**, so the channel can present it directly without assembling anything. The body contains, in order, a level-one title, a summary table, the script content code block and the raw parameters JSON code block. The title, the creator and the risk level are all rendered into it, so the response no longer carries separate structured fields. The summary gives the **impact resolved by the pre-check** (risk level, execute account, the source files and target path of file transfer operations, transfer mode, total execute objects, defaults that took effect, high-risk and dynamic target notices, and so on); per-step details are not expanded in the body, so that an over-long ticket does not push the approver to scroll straight to the bottom and release it. The value of a sensitive field is only a placeholder and never carries the real value. **Script content is the single exception and is shown as is**, otherwise the approver has no way to assess the risk.

The risk level is a hint for the approver only and never takes part in the release check. It is determined as follows:

| Risk level | Condition |
|------|------|
| High | A high-risk statement rule is matched, or there are more than 100 execute objects |
| Medium | There are more than 10 execute objects |
| Low | Everything else |

